.TH AITERM-COMMANDS 7 "2026-10-23" "aiterm 0.9.13-epsilon" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
aiterm-commands \- interactive AITerm command reference
.SH DESCRIPTION
AITerm commands are entered in the AI input line. The leading slash is
optional. Matching is case-insensitive and uses prefix matching against the
command registry; the first matching command wins. For reliable results, type
the complete command words shown below. Some commands open GUI managers or
modify persistent application state.
.SH GENERAL COMMANDS
.TP
.B /help
Show command help.
.TP
.B /legacy help, /extended help
Show alternate help listings where available.
.TP
.B /features, /version, /status, /hw
Show feature information, version, runtime status, or hardware information.
.TP
.B /history, /clear, /directives
Inspect history, clear the AI pane, or display AI directives.
.TP
.B /exit
Exit the application.
.SH TOGGLES
Most toggles accept on, off, or status:
.PP
.nf
/tee on|off|status
/autoreply on|off|status
/autoexe on|off|status
/auto all on|off|status
/autoretry on|off|status
/debug on|off|status
/color on|off|status
/smart cache on|off|status
/ratelimit on|off|status
/rpm <number>
/xml tagging on|off|status
/noise filter on|off|status
/session config on|off|status
/session read from global on|off|status
/session write to global on|off|status
/snmp enable on|off|status
/snmp ticker on|off|status
.fi
.PP
Idle suspension supports the corresponding idle toggle command:
.PP
.nf
/idle on
/idle off
/idle status
.fi
.PP
The exact accepted command spelling is determined by the command registry in
the installed version. Auto All controls Tee, Auto Reply, and Auto Execute
together.
.SH PROVIDER AND CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B /provider
Display provider information.
.TP
.B /list models
List available models where supported.
.TP
.B /load config, /save config
Load or save the application configuration.
.TP
.B /open provider manager
Open the provider manager.
.TP
.B /open provider api keys
Open the provider API-key window.
.SH SESSIONS
.nf
/session new
/session list
/session show
/session sync
/session load <UUID>
/session description <text>
/session default <UUID>
/session no default
/session delete <UUID>
.fi
Session commands can load, inspect, synchronize, describe, select, and delete
saved sessions. Deleting a session can remove persistent data; verify the UUID
before confirming such an operation.
.SH MANAGERS
The following commands open or close their corresponding GUI managers:
.PP
.nf
/open session manager       /close session manager
/open history manager       /close history manager
/open noise manager         /close noise manager
/open policy manager        /close policy manager
/open snmp manager          /close snmp manager
/open provider manager      /close provider manager
.fi
.SH NOISE FILTERING
.nf
/noise filter on|off|status
/noise add <pattern>
/noise list
/noise reload
.fi
.PP
A delete command may appear in help text but is not implemented in every
version. Check the live command help before relying on it.
.SH POLICY COMMANDS
.nf
policy list
policy find <command>
policy add <command|*> <ALLOW|BLOCK|APPROVE> <LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL>
policy delete <command>
.fi
.PP
Policy rules affect automatic command execution. Review rules carefully before
enabling execution features.
.SH SNMP COMMANDS
.nf
/snmp cmd list|add|edit|delete ...
/snmp enable on|off|status
/snmp force
/snmp dump
/snmp poller start|restart
/snmp ticker on|off|status
.fi
.PP
SNMP features depend on the Net-SNMP libraries, configured targets, and
network access.
.SH AI RETRY AND EXECUTION QUEUE
.nf
/retry times <number>
/retry delay <seconds>
/show queue
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Auto-execution can pass AI-generated command payloads into a terminal execution
workflow. Keep execution disabled unless you understand the configured policy,
approval behavior, and trust boundary. Do not run unreviewed AI-generated
commands on systems where mistakes could cause data loss or service disruption.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aiterm (1),
.BR aiterm.conf (5)
